From bd6c7ebbeda158ab17c2cf50aedfc0fed1832c3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: aim Dimension Door only at a known empty floor grid

borg_dimension_door() scores every in-bounds grid in a 100x100 box
around the borg and aims at the one with the lowest danger, without
checking that the player could land there.  The scan starts in the
far north-west corner, so on a normal level the winner is usually a
granite grid the borg has never seen.  The game does not move the
player onto rock: TELEPORT_TO searches outward from the target for
the nearest legal grid, which can be back in the room the borg was
escaping from.

Skip grids the borg does not know to be floor, lava, and grids with a
known monster, so the chosen grid is one the game will accept and the
danger the borg scored is the danger where it lands.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#21.

(cherry picked from commit 4b7a9f414bec7b23aa3453dfb7e54ba2e85c871b)
---
 src/borg/borg-escape.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-escape.c b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
index 51efcc302..0c3a5fa5f 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-escape.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
@@ -575,6 +575,7 @@ bool borg_dimension_door(int allow_fail)
     struct loc best;
     int        d, best_d = 0;
     struct loc target;
+    borg_grid *ag;
 
     /* for now keep the range at under 50, for performance */
     int range = 50;
@@ -601,6 +602,14 @@ bool borg_dimension_door(int allow_fail)
             if (!square_in_bounds_fully(cave, target))
                 continue;
 
+            /* Only aim at a known floor grid without a monster, as the
+             * game moves the player elsewhere when the target is not a
+             * legal landing grid */
+            ag = &borg_grids[t_y][t_x];
+            if (ag->feat == FEAT_NONE || ag->feat == FEAT_LAVA
+                || !borg_cave_floor_grid(ag) || ag->kill)
+                continue;
+
             d = borg_danger(t_y, t_x, 2, true, false);
             if (d < best_d) {
                 best_d = d;
